00:02:54.650 --> 00:02:57.860
episode

00:02:54.650 --> 00:02:57.820
"Cunningly

00:02:54.650 --> 00:02:57.820
and Resiliently !"

00:03:00.750 --> 00:03:02.160
Cardinal Rohan!

00:03:02.450 --> 00:03:04.120
Y-Yes...

00:03:04.420 --> 00:03:07.830
You are saying that I have asked
a lady named Jeanne Valois,

00:03:07.830 --> 00:03:11.080
to make you my guarantor and
purchase that necklace?!

00:03:11.900 --> 00:03:14.600
W-With all due respect, I am speaking the truth.

00:03:14.600 --> 00:03:16.590
Be quiet! Be quiet, Rohan!

00:03:17.000 --> 00:03:19.960
Not only that, you are saying
I met you in secret,

00:03:19.960 --> 00:03:22.660
at the Grove of Venus in the middle
of the night of all things?!

00:03:26.710 --> 00:03:29.440
On what basis are you telling these lies?!

00:03:32.880 --> 00:03:34.150
What is this?!

00:03:34.810 --> 00:03:38.860
P-Please allow me to present the l-love
letters I received from Your Majesty,

00:03:38.860 --> 00:03:41.280
and the contract of sale with your s-signature.

00:03:53.920 --> 00:03:54.940
Cardinal.

00:03:54.940 --> 00:03:57.380
Y-Yes...

00:03:57.980 --> 00:04:00.510
This handwriting is different
from that of the Queen's.

00:04:00.510 --> 00:04:06.350
Also, everyone knows the Queen does not sign
her name as Marie Antoinette de France.

00:04:07.350 --> 00:04:08.940
I-It's a forgery then?!

00:04:09.420 --> 00:04:11.890
Indeed, it's a forgery.

00:04:16.690 --> 00:04:18.000
My King!

00:04:18.000 --> 00:04:19.060
My Queen!

00:04:19.060 --> 00:04:20.800
I beg you!

00:04:20.800 --> 00:04:26.140
I, Rohan, will pay the 1,600,000 livres
for the necklace no matter what!

00:04:26.140 --> 00:04:28.330
S-So please forgive me!

00:04:28.330 --> 00:04:32.810
I was deceived by Jeanne Valois
and her husband Nicolas!

00:04:32.810 --> 00:04:34.040
Please forgive me!

00:04:34.040 --> 00:04:35.170
I beg you...

00:04:36.150 --> 00:04:37.420
Well, my Queen?

00:04:37.420 --> 00:04:41.010
Since it seems the Cardinal was deceived
himself, why don't you forgive him?

00:04:41.390 --> 00:04:42.290
No...

00:04:42.290 --> 00:04:45.620
I'm certain this man, along with
his cohorts, Jeanne and Nicolas,

00:04:45.620 --> 00:04:47.830
plotted this to entrap me!

00:04:47.830 --> 00:04:50.130
But he's apologized, so...

00:04:50.130 --> 00:04:51.020
No...!

00:04:51.020 --> 00:04:55.330
My Mother, Maria Theresa and I despised him
to the point that we wouldn't speak with him.

00:04:55.330 --> 00:04:56.430
This is his revenge...!

00:04:56.430 --> 00:04:57.340
My Queen...

00:04:57.340 --> 00:04:59.170
No, no, I won't forgive him!

00:04:59.170 --> 00:05:01.010
Put him on trial for insulting me!

00:05:01.010 --> 00:05:03.700
Put him on trial, so I can have
my name and honor cleared!

00:05:26.560 --> 00:05:28.120
Welcome.

00:05:28.930 --> 00:05:31.140
Only 10 sous for the night.

00:05:31.140 --> 00:05:33.100
Payment must be made upfront.

00:05:36.910 --> 00:05:38.940
Only 10 sous for the night.

00:05:38.940 --> 00:05:41.040
Payment must be made upfront.

00:05:42.710 --> 00:05:45.650
Monsieur, the payment must be made upfront.

00:05:48.750 --> 00:05:50.490
It's me, Nicole.

00:05:50.490 --> 00:05:51.620
Not a customer.

00:05:53.460 --> 00:05:54.890
That voice...!

00:05:54.890 --> 00:05:56.330
Madame Jeanne Valois!

00:05:56.330 --> 00:05:57.560
It's been a while.

00:05:57.560 --> 00:06:00.800
Thank you for all that money last time.

00:06:00.800 --> 00:06:04.840
About that... It's getting a
little dangerous around me.

00:06:04.840 --> 00:06:09.300
That means, if they find out you impersonated
the Queen, you'll be in danger, as well.

00:06:09.810 --> 00:06:12.540
Here, take this and leave Paris for a while.

00:06:12.540 --> 00:06:14.140
There's about 100 livres in here.

00:06:14.750 --> 00:06:15.610
U-Um...

00:06:15.610 --> 00:06:16.580
Understand?

00:06:16.580 --> 00:06:17.980
As soon as possible.

00:06:30.460 --> 00:06:32.200
Jeanne Valois de la Motte!

00:06:32.200 --> 00:06:35.040
You're under arrest on charges
of forgery, theft and fraud!

00:06:38.870 --> 00:06:42.340
<i>Arrested and charged with forgery of
official documents, theft, fraud...</i>

00:06:42.340 --> 00:06:45.080
<i>...and insulting the royal family,</i>

00:06:45.080 --> 00:06:49.010
<i>everyone involved in the Affair of the
Diamond Necklace, except for Nicolas,</i>

00:06:49.010 --> 00:06:50.800
<i>would soon be put on trial.</i>

00:06:57.100 --> 00:06:59.520
What are you doing in my room, Rosalie?

00:07:03.090 --> 00:07:03.930
It's all right.

00:07:03.930 --> 00:07:06.060
You can play the piano whenever you'd like.

00:07:06.060 --> 00:07:07.170
Um...!

00:07:07.170 --> 00:07:09.580
I've been waiting for your return because
there's something I wanted to ask you.

00:07:11.670 --> 00:07:12.700
What is it?

00:07:12.700 --> 00:07:15.670
Is the crime of insulting the royal
family really serious?

00:07:15.670 --> 00:07:17.500
Does it mean a life sentence or execution?

00:07:19.710 --> 00:07:21.180
Jeanne...

00:07:21.180 --> 00:07:25.500
Jeanne Valois... is my older sister,
who I grew up with in the slums of Paris.

00:07:29.750 --> 00:07:32.150
I never meant to hide it from you.

00:07:32.860 --> 00:07:38.230
I just couldn't bring myself to tell you,
considering what kind of person she is...

00:07:39.960 --> 00:07:41.400
I see...

00:07:42.400 --> 00:07:44.540
But the trial has yet to take place.

00:07:44.540 --> 00:07:48.240
It's not certain that your sister is the culprit yet.

00:07:48.240 --> 00:07:49.910
No, it's not that...!

00:07:49.910 --> 00:07:53.000
I'm not asking you to help her in any way.

00:07:53.510 --> 00:07:56.120
Knowing my sister, I wouldn't put it past her.

00:07:56.510 --> 00:07:58.850
But, um...

00:07:58.850 --> 00:08:00.050
Well...

00:08:00.050 --> 00:08:04.040
If you have an opportunity to see my sister...

00:08:05.090 --> 00:08:07.660
I'd like you to give this ring to her.

00:08:07.660 --> 00:08:09.160
It's Mom's...

00:08:09.160 --> 00:08:11.860
It's a keepsake of our mother...

00:08:12.460 --> 00:08:14.900
I'm plenty happy already,

00:08:14.900 --> 00:08:18.300
so I want my sister Jeanne to have it.

00:08:20.610 --> 00:08:21.770
Done.

00:08:21.770 --> 00:08:23.260
I'll be sure to give it to her.

00:08:24.240 --> 00:08:26.060
Thank you so much...

00:08:26.060 --> 00:08:27.380
Fellow citizens!

00:08:27.380 --> 00:08:30.280
We mustn't view the upcoming
trial as an ordinary case of fraud.

00:08:30.620 --> 00:08:34.420
During the trial, our attention must be
focused on what will be revealed...

00:08:34.420 --> 00:08:36.960
...about the current culture of the
royal family and upper nobility!

00:08:37.520 --> 00:08:42.430
1,600,000 livres, an unfathomable
amount of money to us commoners,

00:08:42.430 --> 00:08:44.400
is the price of just one necklace!

00:08:45.100 --> 00:08:47.930
Such extravagant items come and go
at the Palace of Versailles regularly!

00:08:47.930 --> 00:08:51.390
Not only that, Versailles squanders
our tax money as though it's water!

00:08:51.900 --> 00:08:53.270
Know this, fellow citizens!

00:08:53.270 --> 00:08:56.440
Resentment towards Versailles
is beginning to grow,

00:08:56.440 --> 00:08:59.340
even among the judges of the High Court of Paris!

00:09:00.080 --> 00:09:01.910
Let us hold hope!

00:09:01.910 --> 00:09:05.450
That instead of the crime,
Versailles itself will be put on trial!

00:09:05.450 --> 00:09:07.320
Let us trust the wisdom of
the High Court of Paris!

00:09:08.090 --> 00:09:09.020
That's right!

00:09:09.020 --> 00:09:10.760
It's exactly as Monsieur Robespierre says!

00:09:10.760 --> 00:09:12.740
To Hell with the crime of
insulting the royal family!

00:09:12.740 --> 00:09:13.730
He's right!

00:09:13.730 --> 00:09:15.700
We shouldn't let Versailles
have their way any longer!

00:09:15.700 --> 00:09:17.220
That's right!

00:09:31.840 --> 00:09:32.970
It's from Rosalie.

00:09:33.640 --> 00:09:35.550
She said it was a keepsake of your mother.

00:09:35.550 --> 00:09:37.720
I don't know anyone named Rosalie.

00:09:37.720 --> 00:09:41.620
Plus, I don't wear cheap trinkets. Thanks anyway.

00:09:41.620 --> 00:09:44.480
How do you know it's cheap,
when you haven't even looked at it?

00:09:50.960 --> 00:09:53.930
I promised Rosalie I would give it to you.

00:10:13.480 --> 00:10:15.420
<i>The High Court of Paris</i>

00:10:13.590 --> 00:10:18.180
High Court of Paris

00:10:15.420 --> 00:10:19.750
<i>Even the royal household could not interfere with its internal proceedings.</i>

00:10:27.100 --> 00:10:28.960
Silence, silence!

00:10:30.440 --> 00:10:32.990
I'll ask you one more time,
Jeanne Valois de la Motte.

00:10:33.400 --> 00:10:35.410
No matter how many times you ask,
the answer is the same.

00:10:35.410 --> 00:10:37.540
The one who stole the necklace is Cardinal Rohan.

00:10:37.540 --> 00:10:39.700
I was simply following orders.

00:10:40.410 --> 00:10:43.920
Are you going to keep insisting that you do not know the whereabouts of the necklace?

00:10:44.380 --> 00:10:47.880
Perhaps Cardinal Rohan has already
disposed of it somewhere?

00:10:49.250 --> 00:10:50.250
Jeanne!

00:10:50.250 --> 00:10:51.220
You scoundrel!

00:10:52.660 --> 00:10:54.060
Please be quiet, Cardinal Rohan!

00:10:54.060 --> 00:10:55.560
Where do you think we are?

00:10:55.560 --> 00:10:56.510
This is a courtroom!

00:10:58.260 --> 00:11:02.570
Then, if everything had been
ordered by Cardinal Rohan,

00:11:02.570 --> 00:11:04.970
how do you explain the forged letters
with the Queen's signatures?

00:11:05.400 --> 00:11:09.740
You hired Rétaux de Villette, a phony scrivener
from Paris to write them, didn't you?

00:11:09.740 --> 00:11:11.600
That is what Rétaux said in his confession.

00:11:12.660 --> 00:11:15.740
My, I've never seen this boorish man before.

00:11:15.740 --> 00:11:17.190
<i>Lady Jeanne...</i>

00:11:17.190 --> 00:11:19.700
So you insist on knowing nothing...

00:11:26.660 --> 00:11:27.720
Rosalie, look.

00:11:28.290 --> 00:11:29.500
The ring.

00:11:29.990 --> 00:11:33.460
Your sister is wearing the ring you gave to her.

00:11:34.170 --> 00:11:35.130
Jeanne...

00:11:37.270 --> 00:11:39.830
<i>A little bit is enough. Give me strength, Mom.</i>

00:11:40.400 --> 00:11:42.940
<i>I don't want become a loser
over something like this.</i>

00:11:42.940 --> 00:11:44.440
<i>I want to find a way out of this somehow.</i>

00:11:45.210 --> 00:11:46.410
<i>Because...</i>

00:11:46.410 --> 00:11:50.650
<i>I refuse to let anyone judge me,
even God himself.</i>

00:11:53.420 --> 00:11:56.360
In that case, bring in the witness, Nicole d'Oliva.

00:12:05.000 --> 00:12:06.260
It's the Queen!

00:12:06.260 --> 00:12:07.450
It's Marie Antoinette!

00:12:07.450 --> 00:12:09.400
You idiots. Look closely!

00:12:09.400 --> 00:12:11.370
She looks like the Queen, but she's someone else!

00:12:11.370 --> 00:12:12.900
The Queen wouldn't wear such ragged clothes.

00:12:12.900 --> 00:12:14.270
I guess you're right.

00:12:14.270 --> 00:12:15.970
But she sure looks like her...

00:12:18.340 --> 00:12:19.070
Step out.

00:12:28.550 --> 00:12:30.720
Nicole d'Oliva, well?

00:12:30.720 --> 00:12:33.640
Is this the woman who took
you to the Grove of Venus...

00:12:33.990 --> 00:12:36.480
...and hired you to impersonate the Queen?

00:12:38.400 --> 00:12:40.060
There's no mistaking it.

00:12:40.060 --> 00:12:41.400
It's Madame Jeanne Valois.

00:12:51.640 --> 00:12:52.660
You got me.

00:13:09.460 --> 00:13:11.080
Well then, Jeanne Valois.

00:13:11.080 --> 00:13:17.110
Explain to me why you disguised a prostitute from Paris
as the Queen and took her to the Grove of Venus.

00:13:17.380 --> 00:13:18.060
That's...

00:13:18.410 --> 00:13:19.030
That's?

00:13:19.030 --> 00:13:19.990
That's...

00:13:20.420 --> 00:13:22.610
State your answer promptly!

00:13:22.610 --> 00:13:25.450
The more you lie, the heavier
your sentence shall be!

00:13:26.500 --> 00:13:29.280
I understand... I will tell you everything.

00:13:36.730 --> 00:13:41.340
I truly regret causing
Cardinal Rohan such troubles.

00:13:43.080 --> 00:13:47.700
The Cardinal was merely being
deceived by my husband and I.

00:13:47.700 --> 00:13:50.010
As a matter of fact, regarding this incident,

00:13:50.010 --> 00:13:54.250
a person of high rank, far above Cardinal Rohan, had asked me to carry it out.

00:13:54.250 --> 00:13:57.190
Therefore, we had no other option,
but to go ahead with the scheme.

00:13:57.190 --> 00:14:02.850
The person who asked us to do this, wanted to get that necklace no matter what.

00:14:02.850 --> 00:14:08.160
She is a person who can hold her own, even with
a 1,600,000 livres necklace around her neck.

00:14:08.160 --> 00:14:11.660
She is the Queen of France,
Her Majesty Marie Antoinette!

00:14:15.400 --> 00:14:17.570
Madame Jeanne Valois de la Motte!

00:14:17.570 --> 00:14:21.640
The Queen has said she has no knowledge
of you or the necklace!

00:14:21.640 --> 00:14:23.980
That's exactly why she decided to have this trial!

00:14:23.980 --> 00:14:25.180
Why else?!

00:14:25.180 --> 00:14:27.180
Stop telling such irresponsible lies!

00:14:27.180 --> 00:14:29.500
If you continue to make such accusations
without anything to support it,

00:14:29.500 --> 00:14:33.070
not only will you be tried for insulting the
royal family, but contempt of court, as well!

00:14:33.650 --> 00:14:37.190
The jeweler's complaints were
getting louder by the day,

00:14:37.190 --> 00:14:42.170
so perhaps Her Majesty felt the situation was
becoming a little too precarious for her?

00:14:42.170 --> 00:14:46.530
She called for this trial, so she could
place all the blame on me.

00:14:47.160 --> 00:14:49.030
Show me the evidence first.

00:14:50.740 --> 00:14:57.070
I hear Her Majesty has burned the bill
from Boehmer, the jeweler.

00:14:57.070 --> 00:15:01.210
I'm certain Her Majesty did that
to destroy the evidence!

00:15:01.210 --> 00:15:03.380
Wouldn't you think so, Your Honor?

00:15:03.380 --> 00:15:04.180
She's right!

00:15:04.180 --> 00:15:07.380
If she had nothing to hide, she wouldn't have burned the bill!

00:15:07.380 --> 00:15:09.350
The Queen did it!

00:15:09.350 --> 00:15:11.360
The Queen probably has the necklace!

00:15:11.860 --> 00:15:12.560
That's right!

00:15:12.560 --> 00:15:14.310
The real culprit is that Austrian woman!

00:15:16.290 --> 00:15:18.180
The gallery must stay silent!

00:15:18.180 --> 00:15:20.600
Cause another ruckus and I'll order
the entire gallery to leave the court!

00:15:26.800 --> 00:15:28.240
Madame la Motte.

00:15:28.240 --> 00:15:28.710
Yes.

00:15:28.710 --> 00:15:33.110
The Queen has said she does not know you,
so are you suggesting she is lying?

00:15:33.110 --> 00:15:34.710
That is correct.

00:15:34.710 --> 00:15:39.380
Then state your relationship with the Queen, so that
the court may become convinced.

00:15:39.380 --> 00:15:40.150
Yes.

00:15:41.420 --> 00:15:44.920
Her Majesty had loved me.

00:15:46.390 --> 00:15:48.660
As in... a ''Lesbos'' fashion...

00:15:48.660 --> 00:15:53.360
Well, you see... Her Majesty
has a taste for women.

00:15:53.360 --> 00:15:55.970
I was Her Majesty's lover.

00:16:01.870 --> 00:16:02.600
Jeanne!

00:16:04.840 --> 00:16:07.310
I've never heard of anything of the sort until now.

00:16:07.310 --> 00:16:10.240
Do you have clear evidence to substantiate
this claim, Madame de la Motte?

00:16:10.240 --> 00:16:11.320
Yes.

00:16:11.320 --> 00:16:13.920
I'm sure Your Honor is
aware of Madame Polignac,

00:16:13.920 --> 00:16:18.220
who is well known as Lady Antoinette's favorite?

00:16:18.220 --> 00:16:20.930
She's also someone who is
very dear to Lady Antoinette.

00:16:20.930 --> 00:16:25.190
The most decisive evidence is the Royal Guards'
Commander, Oscar François de Jarjayes.

00:16:27.500 --> 00:16:29.770
She's my husband's, Nicolas' superior,

00:16:29.770 --> 00:16:32.770
and though she dresses like a man,
she's a genuine woman.

00:16:32.770 --> 00:16:38.010
Her Majesty has her lover dress as a man
and keeps her close as a companion.

00:16:38.640 --> 00:16:41.880
Her Majesty Marie Antoinette
is a great, great Queen.

00:16:41.880 --> 00:16:46.990
All the luxuries and pleasures of this world
are hers to keep, and hers alone.

00:16:47.990 --> 00:16:49.190
How dare she...

00:16:48.290 --> 00:16:49.190
Don't, Oscar!

00:16:49.720 --> 00:16:50.720
Calm down!

00:16:50.720 --> 00:16:51.740
This is a courtroom!

00:16:52.060 --> 00:16:53.060
Your Honor!

00:16:53.060 --> 00:16:55.700
I was merely a puppet following orders!

00:16:56.090 --> 00:16:57.860
Judge the Queen before you judge me!

00:16:57.860 --> 00:16:59.660
Marie Antoinette is the one who should be tried!

00:17:00.160 --> 00:17:00.830
She's right!

00:17:00.830 --> 00:17:02.120
The true mastermind is the Queen!

00:17:02.430 --> 00:17:03.730
An adulterer and a lesbian!

00:17:03.730 --> 00:17:06.090
The culprit has to be that Austrian whore!

00:17:06.540 --> 00:17:07.740
Jeanne Valois!

00:17:07.740 --> 00:17:08.720
I'm on your side!

00:17:14.920 --> 00:17:16.410
The court is adjourned! The court is adjourned!

00:17:16.410 --> 00:17:18.570
The court will be adjourned for a while!

00:17:19.720 --> 00:17:20.680
I see.

00:17:20.680 --> 00:17:23.190
What a spectacular trial, Monsieur Robespierre.

00:17:23.690 --> 00:17:28.650
Indeed, the royal family couldn't
have been more disgraced.

00:17:29.490 --> 00:17:31.730
Come, let's leave here, Saint-Just.

00:17:31.730 --> 00:17:32.760
Yes.

00:17:32.760 --> 00:17:36.770
<i>This young man is Saint-Just, during
his youthful days as a law student.</i>

00:17:36.770 --> 00:17:40.620
<i>This young revolutionist would later become
Robespierre's closest confidant.</i>

00:17:41.270 --> 00:17:47.140
<i>Also, the journalist who follows Robespierre
like a shadow is Bernard Châtelet.</i>

00:17:47.140 --> 00:17:51.440
<i>He, too, was a young man with a
burning passion for the new era.</i>

00:17:51.440 --> 00:17:55.250
<i>"The Affair of the Diamond Necklace" was
the incident that clearly instilled resentment,</i>

00:17:55.250 --> 00:17:58.920
<i>among the populace and particularly among
the younger generation, towards the old regime.</i>

00:17:58.920 --> 00:18:03.520
<i>This incident was the catalyst that eventually
culminated into the French Revolution.</i>

00:18:04.530 --> 00:18:06.260
How could she say such awful things...

00:18:07.100 --> 00:18:09.230
I'm sorry, Lady Oscar...

00:18:09.230 --> 00:18:12.670
My sister said all those things because
she was desperate to save herself...!

00:18:14.010 --> 00:18:16.700
She's resilient... Such a resilient spirit.

00:18:17.210 --> 00:18:21.350
Even while she stood at the edge
of a cliff, she didn't reel back.

00:18:21.350 --> 00:18:22.660
In fact, she even seemed composed.

00:18:23.000 --> 00:18:24.480
Jeanne...

00:18:24.480 --> 00:18:27.790
I've never seen a woman like her...

00:18:32.290 --> 00:18:36.930
<i>On Wednesday, May 31, 1786,</i>

00:18:36.930 --> 00:18:41.260
<i>the High Court of Paris handed down
the sentences on the necklace theft.</i>

00:18:41.260 --> 00:18:43.500
Captain Nicolas de la Motte.

00:18:43.500 --> 00:18:47.470
Although on the run, he is hereby sentenced
to the galleys for life, in absentia.

00:18:47.470 --> 00:18:49.640
He is to be arrested immediately when found.

00:18:49.640 --> 00:18:50.880
Rétaux de Villette.

00:18:50.880 --> 00:18:54.200
You are hereby sentenced to exile from France
for 35 years, after receiving 50 lashes.

00:18:55.210 --> 00:18:57.200
Nicole d'Oliva. Not guilty.

00:18:58.250 --> 00:19:00.160
Madame Jeanne Valois de la Motte.

00:19:00.750 --> 00:19:05.120
You are hereby sentenced to life in prison after being
branded on both shoulders with the letter V{ by a branding iron}.

00:19:07.020 --> 00:19:09.000
Cardinal Louis de Rohan.

00:19:09.000 --> 00:19:12.300
On the charges of your involvement in the necklace
theft and insulting the royal family...

00:19:12.300 --> 00:19:13.190
Not guilty.

00:19:18.340 --> 00:19:20.260
Your Honor, please answer my question!

00:19:20.600 --> 00:19:24.260
What about the true mastermind?!
The mastermind who gave me the order?!

00:19:24.260 --> 00:19:27.270
Are you just going to punish
me and look the other way?!

00:19:27.270 --> 00:19:30.450
The High Court does not judge
people on assumptions alone.

00:19:30.450 --> 00:19:33.820
Even if, by chance, there is a true
mastermind behind this case as you say...

00:19:33.820 --> 00:19:36.190
Just as the royal household
cannot interfere with the court,

00:19:36.190 --> 00:19:40.200
neither can the court interfere
with the royal household.

00:19:42.030 --> 00:19:44.700
But that makes it sound as
though I were the mastermind!

00:19:44.700 --> 00:19:46.030
Labeled as a lesbian...?!

00:19:46.030 --> 00:19:47.230
Labeled as the mastermind...?!

00:19:47.230 --> 00:19:49.230
Not only that, Rohan was found innocent?!

00:19:49.230 --> 00:19:52.170
What was the point of going
ahead with the trial then?!

00:19:52.170 --> 00:19:54.310
My poor Queen...

00:19:54.310 --> 00:19:55.470
Madame Polignac...

00:19:55.470 --> 00:19:56.440
Tell me...

00:19:56.440 --> 00:19:58.590
What have I done to deserve all this...?

00:20:00.080 --> 00:20:01.010
It makes me so angry...!

00:20:01.010 --> 00:20:02.140
Your Majesty...

00:20:03.350 --> 00:20:05.550
What an odd incident though.

00:20:05.550 --> 00:20:10.020
To think that a member of the Royal Guards of
all people, would cause such a misconduct.

00:20:10.020 --> 00:20:14.780
Also, how could the Regiment Commander not have
realized, that a subordinate was plotting to flee?

00:20:15.890 --> 00:20:18.320
No, it's nothing, Your Majesty.

00:20:22.400 --> 00:20:24.820
<i>A month after the sentences
had been handed down,</i>

00:20:24.820 --> 00:20:28.200
<i>Jeanne's punishment was carried out
while the people of Paris looked on.</i>

00:20:29.540 --> 00:20:34.140
<i>A branding iron with the letter V,
taken from the French word for thief.</i>

00:20:37.250 --> 00:20:38.590
Damn it!

00:20:53.560 --> 00:20:55.200
Let me go! I'm innocent!

00:20:55.200 --> 00:20:56.690
The Queen plotted everything!

00:20:57.170 --> 00:20:58.770
She placed all the blame me!

00:20:59.240 --> 00:21:00.490
Yet she's—!

00:21:05.810 --> 00:21:08.080
Damn you to Hell, Marie Antoinette!

00:21:08.080 --> 00:21:09.640
I'm innocent!

00:21:15.500 --> 00:21:19.310
Damn it, what a hellcat! She bit my arm open!

00:21:18.620 --> 00:21:20.990
Look, she fainted with her eyes open.

00:21:20.990 --> 00:21:23.010
Take her to the prison inside
Salpêtrière immediately.

00:21:23.010 --> 00:21:23.470
Yes!

00:21:23.010 --> 00:21:23.470
Yes!

00:21:29.680 --> 00:21:34.070
<i>Jeanne's masterful lies gathered the support
and sympathies from the whole country.</i>

00:21:34.070 --> 00:21:36.510
<i>Every day, Salpêtrière where
Jeanne was imprisoned,</i>

00:21:36.510 --> 00:21:39.660
<i>was flooded with people who
wished to get a glimpse of her.</i>

00:21:40.340 --> 00:21:42.210
How could this be happening?

00:21:42.210 --> 00:21:46.150
I hear not only commoners, but even
nobles are visiting to see Jeanne.

00:21:46.150 --> 00:21:47.150
Yes.

00:21:47.750 --> 00:21:49.820
Why would a noble with rank and title visit her?

00:21:49.820 --> 00:21:51.120
I don't understand it.

00:21:51.460 --> 00:21:56.770
I regret to inform you that those nobles
are the ones who left the court,

00:21:56.770 --> 00:21:59.260
after they were denied access
to Your Majesty's villa.

00:22:00.800 --> 00:22:03.420
But... for something so inconsequential as that...?

00:22:15.510 --> 00:22:17.150
It sure was fun...

00:22:17.150 --> 00:22:19.410
It's been so long, it gave me the chills...

00:22:22.850 --> 00:22:28.690
I always wanted to pull a prank
like that when I was a child...

00:22:28.690 --> 00:22:29.950
...with everyone...

00:22:29.740 --> 00:22:33.460
To be continued

